course: dictionary
lesson: 3776
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the context: the words and sentences around it. «Change the font to Arial and make the title bold.» The clues are change, Arial and bold, so font means a set of letters in one design.
explain: «The baby was baptised at the font near the church door.» The clues are baby, baptised and church, so font means the large stone or wooden basin that holds water. The same word can mean something very different in a different setting.
explain: Font can also mean a source of something, as in «a font of knowledge». Swap in the word source to check: «a source of knowledge» still makes sense, so this is the right meaning. Always test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Font has three main meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant.
fact: On a computer, a font is a set of letters and numbers in one design and size, such as Arial or Times New Roman.
fact: In a church, a font is a large stone or wooden basin that holds the water for baptism, often near the door.
fact: As a formal word, a font is a source of something, such as «a font of wisdom». The spelling «fount» means the same.
exercise: «Change the font to Arial and make the heading bigger.» What does font mean here? | * A set of letters and numbers in one design and size | A large stone bowl for water in a church | A small picture on a screen | A source of knowledge
exercise: «The baby was baptised at the font near the church door.» What is the font? | A set of letters for a computer | A plain room for the choir | * A large stone or wooden basin that holds water for baptism | A tall wooden chair
exercise: «She is a font of knowledge about dinosaurs.» What does font mean in this sentence? | * A source of something, here facts about dinosaurs | A colour printed on paper | A bold heading | A lot of mud
test: «Her father is a font of wisdom.» What does font mean? | A stone bowl for water | * A source of wisdom | A bold, large style of letters | A door in a church
test: «The lectern and the font stood at the front of the church.» What is the font? | A computer design | * A large stone basin for water | A row of wooden seats | A set of letters and numbers
exam: «The font on the poster was hard to read, so the teacher asked for a new font.» In this sentence, font means? | A church basin for water | * A set of letters and numbers in one design and size | A source of knowledge | A stone pulpit for preaching
